I'd say 'few' is sometimes now traslating 'too many'

CentOS-3: ia64, s390, s390x
CentOS-4: ia64, s390, s390x, alpha, sparc

And i have weird fixation about PA-RISC on my head too, but fortunately
i don't have even suitable hardware available ,-)

Generally i have moved a lot towards of these 'out of upstream'
versions lately (namely alpha, sparc), but i do obey my bounds to 'you
support what you have released' for other arches too.

This is a good as any point to mention, that i did think very carefully
before i even did made any alpha/axp version publically available, that
i do have to take care of it 5-6 years worst (or find someone other to
take care of it).


